Package: piproxyguard
Version: __VERSION__
Architecture: __ARCH__
Maintainer: TheMysteriousStranger90 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: squid-openssl | squid, jq, adduser, sudo
Recommends: iptables, netfilter-persistent, openssl
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/TheMysteriousStranger90/PiProxyGuard
Description: Squid proxy traffic statistics and protection for Raspberry Pi
 PiProxyGuard ingests Squid access logs into SQLite, serves a Blazor dashboard
 and REST API on port 5080, maintains a domain blocklist and detects anomalies.
 .
 Installing this package pulls in Squid, writes a working squid.conf, creates
 the service user and starts the API and Worker systemd services automatically.
 The binaries are self-contained, so no .NET runtime is required.
 .
 Optional whole-LAN (transparent) interception can be enabled with
 'piproxyguard-transparent enable' (or PIPROXYGUARD_TRANSPARENT=1 at install):
 it configures Squid intercept ports, iptables redirects and IP forwarding so
 the blocklist applies to every device routed through the Pi, blocking HTTPS by
 SNI without decryption.
